  {
   "type": "textmedia",
   "header": "<h1> Tooth by Tooth in the Focus of the Probe </h1>",
   "body": "<p>The electronic measuring probe supplements the ZOLLER sensor system for measurements on undercut surfaces to determine form and position deviations of the rake faces, pitch of the flutes and flute direction. Thanks to its integrated CNC Y-axis, the »hobCheck« optics carrier offers unique possibilities for the economical complete measurement of straight-fluted and helical gear cutting tools.</p>",
   "images": [
    {
     "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/3/3/csm_Zahn-um-zahn_66e500702d.webp",
     "alt": "",
     "w": 1454,
     "h": 1454
    }
   ],
   "videos": [],
   "pos": "right",
   "cols": 1,
   "valign": "center",
   "ftype": "textmedia",
   "id": "c2081",
   "bg": "black",
   "space": {
    "before": "extra-large",
    "after": "extra-large"
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "tiles",
   "header": "<h3> Measuring Programs </h3>",
   "cols": 4,
   "tiles": [
    {
     "logo": {
      "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/0/b/csm_Switchcard313_9246b53dc5.webp",
      "alt": "",
      "w": 590,
      "h": 590
     },
     "label": "Solutions for insert-tipped milling cutters Measuring program 313",
     "img": null,
     "text": "<h4><strong>Measuring program 313</strong></h4> <p><img alt=\"\" height=\"606\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/fileadmin/_processed_/5/6/csm_Messprogramm_313_de_8686acad0c.webp\" title=\"\" width=\"1024\"/></p> <p>for measuring insert-tipped cylindrical hobs with comprehensive evaluation based on DIN 3968. Among other things, concentricity deviation at the tooth head, individual and cumulative pitch and pitch jump of the flutes, flute direction, tooth thickness, cutter pitch height are determined.</p>"
    },
    {
     "logo": {
      "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/4/6/csm_switchcard314_7a0baefbc4.webp",
      "alt": "",
      "w": 590,
      "h": 590
     },
     "label": "Solutions for insert-tipped milling cutters Measuring program 314",
     "img": null,
     "text": "<h4><strong>Measuring program 314</strong></h4> <h4><img alt=\"\" height=\"606\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/fileadmin/_processed_/b/9/csm_Messprogramm_314_de_45e8dd3ccb.webp\" title=\"\" width=\"1024\"/></h4> <p>for measuring tooth form cutters with comprehensive evaluation based on DIN 3968. Among other things, concentricity deviation at the tooth tip, individual and total pitch and pitch jump of the flutes, flute direction, tooth thickness, pressure angle 1 and 2 are determined.</p>"
    },
    {
     "logo": {
      "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/7/1/csm_switchcard315_verh_015b7d945f.webp",
      "alt": "",
      "w": 590,
      "h": 590
     },
     "label": "Inspection of protuberance and tooth flanks Measuring program 315",
     "img": null,
     "text": "<h4><strong>Measuring program 315</strong></h4> <p><img alt=\"\" height=\"606\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/fileadmin/_processed_/0/0/csm_Messprogramm_315_de_f67a7e93cd.webp\" title=\"\" width=\"1024\"/></p> <p>for measuring the protuberance on cylindrical hobs. The protuberance amount, height and angle as well as the edge breakage height on the left and right tooth flank are determined.</p>"
    },
    {
     "logo": {
      "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/1/a/csm_Switchcard720_verh_1738caa3fc.webp",
      "alt": "",
      "w": 590,
      "h": 590
     },
     "label": "Inspection of protuberance and tooth flanks Measuring program 720",
     "img": null,
     "text": "<h4><strong>Measuring program 720</strong></h4> <p><img alt=\"\" height=\"606\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/fileadmin/_processed_/4/e/csm_Messprogramm_720_de_96b30bcea9.webp\" title=\"\" width=\"1024\"/></p> <p>for measuring the axial relief on the tooth flanks of hobs. The exact contour of the relief is recorded and analyzed with the scanning probe.</p>"
    },
    {
     "logo": {
      "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/9/b/csm_switchcard412_8c749a9293.webp",
      "alt": "",
      "w": 590,
      "h": 590
     },
     "label": "Efficiently inspect cutting and skiving gears Measuring program 412",
     "img": null,
     "text": "<h4>Measuring program 412</h4> <p><img alt=\"\" height=\"606\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/fileadmin/_processed_/e/1/csm_Messprogramm_412_de_79bd895409.webp\" title=\"\" width=\"1024\"/></p> <p>for tactile measurement of cutting wheels with measuring probe and evaluation according to DIN 1829. Straight and helical cutting wheels can be measured. The axial run-out, rake angle at the tooth tip and the rake face pitch angle (for helical cutting wheels) are determined.</p>"
    },
    {
     "logo": {
      "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/f/a/csm_switchcard512_d6fc475546.webp",
      "alt": "",
      "w": 590,
      "h": 590
     },
     "label": "Efficiently inspect cutting and skiving gears Measuring program 512",
     "img": null,
     "text": "<h4><strong>Measuring program 512</strong></h4> <p><img alt=\"\" height=\"606\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/fileadmin/_processed_/e/3/csm_Messprogramm_512_de_61f562af27.webp\" title=\"\" width=\"1024\"/></p> <p>for the measurement of hobbing gears in transmitted and incident light with evaluation according to DIN 1829. The program determines concentricity deviation on the pitch and tip circle, individual pitch deviation left/right, pitch step left/right, total pitch deviation left/right, tooth thickness variation, rake angle on the tooth tip and the rake face pitch angle.</p>"
    },
    {
     "logo": {
      "src": "/fileadmin/_processed_/7/6/csm_switchcard482_eabfc04a63.webp",
      "alt": "",
      "w": 590,
      "h": 590
     },
     "label": "Precise wear control on milling cutters Measuring program 482",
     "img": null,
     "text": "<h4><strong>Measuring program 482</strong></h4> <p><img alt=\"\" height=\"606\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/fileadmin/_processed_/7/6/csm_Messprogramm_482_de_9b5c02f50d.webp\" title=\"\" width=\"1024\"/></p> <p>for automatic image acquisition of the teeth on the circumference and in the chip space of cylindrical hobs. Display of the cutting edge images including measuring function for quick and easy determination of the greatest wear. This enables the resharpening process to be optimized and ensures that neither too much nor too little resharpening is carried out.</p>"
    }
   ],
